# Bundled beatmaps: the fresh-install payload of typebeat.Desktop/Bundled/.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The packages themselves carry real, non-redistributable audio, so
# typebeat.Desktop/Bundled/ is gitignored and always will be. That left the bundle recorded
# NOWHERE: the Windows release shipped whatever .typb happened to sit in one machine's working
# tree, and the Linux/macOS CI builds, starting from a fresh actions/checkout where the directory
# does not exist, shipped none at all and said nothing about it. This manifest is the record.
# It names the bundle and pins every package by sha256, and it carries no audio, so it can live
# in git.
#
# WHO READS IT.
#   .github/scripts/bundled-maps.sh   populates Bundled/ in CI before the publish, and verifies
#   ship-client.ps1                   verifies the local Bundled/ before the Windows pack
# Both treat any mismatch as fatal. A build that cannot satisfy this manifest must not produce an
# installer: an installer with a silently empty bundle is the exact defect this file prevents,
# and it shipped for an unknown number of releases before anyone noticed.
#
# FORMAT. One entry per line, comments and blank lines ignored:
#
#     <sha256>  <size in bytes>  <file name>
#
# The file name is the rest of the line, so it may contain spaces; sha256 is lowercase hex. The
# name is the on-disk name under Bundled/ and is also what the game imports, so renaming an entry
# here renames the shipped package.
#
# TRANSPORT. Fetches are content-addressed off the hash in column 1:
#
#     https://typebeat.sh/releases/bundled-<sha256>.typb
#
# served by the web app's existing anonymous /releases/{file} route out of
# /data/downloads/releases/ inside the app container. Content addressing means the checksum IS
# the URL: fetching bytes that do not match the manifest would mean fetching a URL nobody
# published, so the two can never silently disagree.
#
# CHANGING THE BUNDLE. Add or replace the .typb in Bundled/, then:
#   0. python .github/scripts/bundled-maps-online.py
#      proves every package is the SITE's current copy of a ranked set (an older download
#      imports as a different map with no leaderboard) and lists the intro beatdrop candidates
#   1. .github/scripts/bundled-maps.sh manifest > typebeat.Desktop/bundled-maps.manifest
#   2. upload the new package to the box under its content-addressed name (see the script header
#      for the exact command), or the next CI build fails
#   3. commit the regenerated manifest
# Order matters: the upload must land before the manifest reaches a branch CI builds from.

